### Stack Overgram Backend

The Stack Overgram leverages MongoDB and Express to build a REST API. The core entities are
Questions, Comments, Answers, and Tags. The new entities added in this project are Users,
Notifications, Badges, and Follows.

API requests are initially handled in the controller layer where input validation occurs and
appropriate HTTP status responses are provided. Business logic is contained within the
`application.ts` file. Tests are written for both the controller and application layers.

#### Entities

- Questions: Represents questions asked by users.
- Comments: Represents comments made on questions or answers.
- Answers: Represents answers to questions.
- Tags: Represents tags associated with questions.
- Users: Represents users of the application.
- Notifications: Represents notifications sent to users.
- Badges: Represents badges awarded to users.
- Follows: Represents follow relationships between users.

#### API Endpoints

The API endpoints are organized by entity and follow RESTful conventions. List of routes:

`/question`

- `GET /getQuestion` - gets questions with provided filters
- `GET /getQuestionById/:qid` - gets question with the given question ID
- `POST /addQuestion` - adds the provided question
- `POST /upvoteQuestion` - upvotes the provided question
- `POST /downvoteQuestion` - downvotes the provided question

The following endpoints were newly created for this project:

- `GET /askedBy/:username` - gets questions asked by the provided user
- `GET /answeredBy/:username` - gets questions answered by the provided user
- `GET /upvotedBy/:username` - gets questions upvoted by the provided user
- `GET /downvotedBy/:username` - gets questions downvoted by the provided user

`/answer`

- `POST /addAnswer` - posts the provided answer to the provided question

`/comment`

- `POST /addComment` - posts the provided comment to the provided question or answer

`/tag`

- `GET /getTagsWithQuestionNumber` - gets tags with their associated questions
- `GET /getTagByName/:name` - gets a tag by its name

`/user`

All of the following endpoints were created for this project.

- `POST /` - creates the provided user in MongoDB and Firebase
- `POST /login` - logs the user in, verifying their identity through Firebase
- `POST /logout` - logs the provided user out
- `GET /:username` - gets the user with the requested username
- `PATCH /:username` - updates the provided user
- `POST /follow` - creates a follow record
- `GET /follow/:username` - gets the followers and following list of the provided user
- `GET /follow/recommendations/:username` - gets recommended users for the provided user to follow
- `GET /feed/:username` - gets a following activity feed for the provided user

`/notification`

All of the following endpoints were created for this project.

- `GET /:username` - gets the notifications of the provided user
- `PATCH /seen/:username` - updates the provided user's notifications as "seen"
- `DELETE /:username/:notificationId` - deletes the given notification for the given user

#### Real-time Updates

Real-time updates are handled using WebSockets. The controllers contain a socket and emit typed
events to send real-time notifications to users when certain events occur (e.g., new comments,
answers, or follows).

#### Setup and Installation

1. Clone the repository and navigate to the server directory

   `git clone https://github.com/neu-cs4530/fall24-team-project-group-112.git`

   `cd server `

2. Install dependences `npm install`

3. Set up environment variables by creating a .env file in the /server directory. Add the secrets
   provided by our project group.

4. Run the server:

   `npm run start` or `npm run start:dev` for hot reloading

5. Access the API: The API will be available at `http://localhost:3000`
